{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"1f013f6426b27f8cb555c22229b6c039f0c3bf25e128f377b49ae37cdbaeeacb","digest":{"component_or_area":"Jira reconcile-bridge outbound comment sync","key_entities":["REB-1861","REB-1580","REB-1829","comment_ids","RECONCILER_MARKER","outbound_comments._normalize_comment_body","_TRUNCATION_SUFFIX","adf.adf_to_text","GET /rest/api/3/issue/{key}/comment","DELETE /rest/api/3/issue/{key}/comment/{id}","712020:6471376f-4e5e-4ed2-8c05-330827bc387e","aa7b-5e47-6d3d-4615","irongrey-chubby-oxpecker","bd80-0603-7d44-4d9f","adapters/jira/comment_limits.py","outbound_comments.py",".github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml","run 32403944666"],"problem_keywords":["duplicate comments","jira reconciliation","data cleanup","outbound comment sync","comment deduplication","bot echo","rate limiting"],"propositions":["The Jira reconcile-bridge bug aa7b-5e47-6d3d-4615 left the comment-id dedup map inert, causing duplicate comments to be re-posted on every hourly pass until the workflow was paused.","REB-1861 reached Jira's 5000-comment hard cap; 30 affected issues collectively hold 31,683 comments with 30,847 marked as reconciler bot-authored duplicates.","A cleanup operation deterministically identified 29,931 duplicate bot comments via marker detection on pre-strip ADF text, kept one copy per distinct normalized body (oldest by created timestamp), and deleted the rest via rate-limit-aware REST calls with full pre-deletion backup and independent post-deletion verification.","Phase 1 deleted 29,931 comments across 27 issues with zero failures; REB-1861 dropped from 5000 to 79 comments; all surviving distinct bodies were independently verified against 150MB pre-deletion backups with zero missing bodies and unchanged non-candidate counts.","836 unmarked comments across REB-1567, REB-1931, and REB-2605 carry the reconciler's own truncation suffix and were deliberately held for phase 2 decision with --include-truncated flag, as they require a derived truncation-based identifier rule rather than the marker-based precedent.","The reconcile-bridge workflow remains paused and was not re-enabled by this ticket; a separate defect (marker truncation at 32767 chars) that defeated loop-breaker detection was identified and reported for repair."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787479204513631001,"uuid":"275f0a88-a6fb-4942-9f0a-1d6a5b339ec5"}